 "result": "This is all in `src/tessel/views.py`, split between two classes.\n\n**`View`** (L16) turns the class into a view function.\n- `View.to_view_func(name, ...)` (L86) is a classmethod that returns a plain function `view(**kwargs)`.\n  - By default it builds a new instance per request, or one shared instance if `init_every_request = False`, and calls `self.run_view(**kwargs)` through `active_app.ensure_sync`.\n  - It applies any `decorators`.\n  - It sets `__name__` and copies `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` onto the function. It also sets `view_class` on the function, which `attach_route_rule` can use to register the allowed methods.\n\n**`VerbView`** (L138) maps HTTP methods to handlers.\n- `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (L165) sets `cls.methods` automatically. It collects uppercase names for each `http_method_funcs` entry that the class defines (`get`, `post`, and so on) and merges in base-class `methods`.\n- `VerbView.run_view` (L182) is the dispatcher.\n  - It calls `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and invokes it with the URL kwargs via `ensure_sync`.\n  - A `HEAD` request falls back to `get` if there is no `head` method.\n  - If no handler exists it hits an `assert`.\n\nYou register it with `app.attach_route_rule(\"/path\", view_func=MyView.to_view_func(\"name\"))`.",
